 "lines": "when words / are read aloud— / & sung alone as / gospels to the lonely / mirror's / midnight hours— / that left tears / drying with time / that has come / & too passed—",
 "read": "When words are read aloud and sung alone as gospels to the lonely mirror's midnight hours, the left tears drying with time that is common to past. We can embrace a new day. We can receive a new day. We can welcome a new day.",
